# Tray runs the AirDrop BLE beacon automatically (2026-10-31 01:42-01:51)

## why
Measured tonight: with the beacon advertising, the same 29 MB video ran 1.09-1.10 MB/s
at 867-970 fps and CRC 3.4-4.2%; every run without it sat at 0.32-0.88 MB/s, 313-788 fps,
CRC 12.8-49.3%. iOS keeps AWDL asleep until its share sheet is open or a device sends the
AirDrop BLE advertisement, so the beacon is what keeps the phone on our schedule.

## what was added
src\beacon\airdrop-beacon.ps1   upstream winawdl script (MIT), copied verbatim
backend\beacon.ps1              what the package ships
TrayApp: StartBeacon/StopBeacon/CheckBeacon/ToggleBeacon
  - started with the tray, restarted by the 5 s watchdog if it dies, killed on exit
  - output appended to data\logs\<session>\beacon.log
  - menu item "蓝牙 beacon（帮 iPhone 发现这台电脑）", on by default; turning it off
    writes data\beacon-off so a deliberate choice survives restarts
  - missing script or no usable Bluetooth adapter only logs, never blocks receiving

## verified
tray start at 01:42:37: beacon.log shows "advertising" 0.4 s after the chain started,
so the publisher is up before the radio finishes its own bring-up.

## NOT verified: the radio never came up in these runs
Both attempts (01:42 and 01:47) left airbridge_radio.exe at 0.03 s CPU for 3-4 minutes
with not a single devourer line in radio.log: the process is blocked inside a libusb
call. This is the wedged-USB state the runbook describes, reached by force-killing the
radio repeatedly tonight. Recovery is a physical replug; it is NOT a defect introduced by
the beacon (the beacon only talks to Bluetooth, and it printed advertising while the
radio was already stuck).

Two gaps this exposes, both worth fixing next:
1. A hung radio looks alive to the supervisor (process exists), so the watchdog never
   reacts. A silence check is needed: the radio writes a stats line every ~5 s even idle,
   so >30 s without one means hung -> restart the chain, and if that repeats, tell the
   user to replug instead of looping.
2. Forced kills leave children alive holding 49876/49877/8771 (Q55).
